From tille at debian.org  Tue May  8 10:33:23 2018
From: tille at debian.org (Andreas Tille)
Date: Tue, 8 May 2018 12:33:23 +0200
Subject: When beeing bored by new package dependencies [Was: dh-r_20180508_source.changes ACCEPTED into unstable]
Message-ID: <20180508103323.xsouxrjjo75zrjch@an3as.eu>

Hi,

since I was routinely bored when my routine-update script failed due to
new dependencies I wrote a script prepare_missing_cran_package that
fetches this dependency and fires up dh-make-R.  It works recursively if
the missing dependencies has other missing dependencies.  You can trigger
the script by

    dh-update-R (tested with r-cran-blockmodeling, r-cran-ddalpha, r-cran-httpuv)
    dh-make-R   (untested)

It puts the packaging attempts into ../CRAN_prospective.

Please test, comment and most favourably fix if anything does not work
as expected.

Kind regards

      Andreas.

